# Trust policy for markovianprotocol.com/log (c2sp.org/tlog-policy)
#
# A checkpoint is valid if it is signed by the log and cosigned by at
# least 4 of the 7 pinned witnesses below -- the same quorum the log's
# own standing monitor enforces (github.com/MarkovianProtocol/log-monitor).
# Every key below was collected from the witness operator's own published
# key page, not from this log.
#
# Honest note: little-garden and ring-any-bells are both operated by
# TrustFabric (Google). The 4-of-7 quorum cannot be met by any single
# operator's keys alone.
#
# A signature under this log's own origin name (markovianprotocol.com/log)
# never counts toward the witness quorum, whatever its algorithm. The log
# signs its own checkpoints with Ed25519 and ML-DSA-44; those lines
# authenticate the checkpoint, they are not witness cosignatures.

